<title>USA: BPA offers 200 MW peak firm power for Monday.</title>
<headline>BPA offers 200 MW peak firm power for Monday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration  (BPA) offered 200 megawatts (MW) of peak firm power for Monday pre-schedulings,  but did not offer any power over the weekend, the agency said Friday.</p>
<p>BPA priced the Monday offer at $22.00 per megawatt hour (MWh) for  Northwest sales and $23.00 for California-Oregon border (COB) sales.</p>
<p>BPA has been out of the surplus daily market since the beginning of  the week amid refilling of reservoirs ahead of April fish flow requirements.</p>
<p>The agency said earlier it expected outflows to pick up again next  week.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau, +1 213 955 6761))</p>
